    {
      "id": "fa797f20-dceb-490a-bf2d-1d2f7bd36aa8",
      "name": "Sticky Note f5f1deab",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Automation 05: Feedback Logging and Escalation\n\n### Introduction\nLogs every customer feedback form in one register, replies to the customer straight away and alerts the manager about low ratings. No AI is used.\n\n### What to key in\nThe customer fills in **Feedback Form**: Account Number, Email, Score from 1 to 5, and Comment.\nAfter a callback, staff set status to Closed and fill resolved_at in the **Register** tab.\n\n### What happens next\n1. The answers are tidied and saved in the **Register** tab.\n2. Score 2 or below: the manager is alerted, and the customer gets an apology with a reference number.\n3. Score 3 or above: the customer gets a thank-you note.\n4. Each weekday at 9am, the manager is reminded about any open case past its callback time.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect your Gmail account in all four Gmail nodes.\n2. In **Config** and **Reminder Config**, enter the manager details and company name.\n3. Test with test_mode on in both, which sends every email to test_email.\n4. For live use, set test_mode to false in both, then publish.\n5. Share the Production URL from **Feedback Form** with customers.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 720
      }
    }
